{
  "name": "276. Warp keeps embedding spaces apart and counts what a turn embedded (warp-preservation) [SERIAL]",
  "description": "TXE-5543 regression. Local fixture regression: run with warpWire=1 and warpWireFixtureUrl against the gateway of tests/e2e/api/provider_config/warp-wire.config.json, with a logs store and a vector store, and tests/e2e/api/runners/warp-wire-fixture.mjs as the only upstream. A retired namespace holds vectors of a space nothing records, so moving back onto one is refused; clearing the space in place is refused, and clearing it onto a new namespace retires the old one. A turn that searches reports its model calls and each query embedding once: 110 tokens per model call and 7 per embedding on this fixture. Model turns held open, backfill pages, tied timestamps and the chart, trace and search reads cannot be sent from a collection: tests/e2e/api/runners/run-warp-wire.mjs covers them. Run the whole folder in order.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "[setup] the warp feature flag is on - warp-preservation",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/feature-flags"
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.variables.get('warpWire') !== '1') {",
              "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
              "}",
              "var stamp = Date.now();",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('warpPresA', 'Warppres' + stamp + 'a');",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('warpPresB', 'Warppres' + stamp + 'b');",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('warpPresC', 'Warppres' + stamp + 'c');",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('warpPresD', 'Warppres' + stamp + 'd');"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('warp-preservation: warp flag enabled', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'failed: ' + pm.response.text()).to.equal(200);",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().flags.filter(function (f) { return f.id === 'warp' && f.enabled; }).length, pm.response.text()).to.equal(1);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
